# 🎉 Python Fun Fact

Before modern packaging tools became popular, **`setup.py`** was the standard way to build and distribute Python packages. You'll still find it in many existing open-source projects.

---

# 🔄 Quick Recap

- `setup.py` stores package metadata.
- It defines information like the package name and version.
- It helps prepare projects for distribution.
- Understanding package metadata is an important developer skill.

